          "why": "drift 0.13"
        }
      ],
      "transcript": "Now, how does this map to be clear to the real world? Well, we can't see the tiny little switches inside of our Mac's, PCs, and our phones that are actually turning the electricity on or off, storing electricity or not. But they're called transistors. They've got like millions of them in today's hardware. And they're just on or off like a switch or a light bulb."
    },
